  "claim_boundary": "This source-pinned, failure-inclusive development packet measures one generic axis-mode-denoise family on the immutable 20 ARC1 plus 20 ARC2 filename-only development cohort. For each visible example or test input, it independently derives row and column line modes, compares total modal support (equivalent to average line purity), and fills each line along the uniquely more-supported axis. It refuses modal-color and axis-support ties rather than silently using an arbitrary color or orientation. P0014 is the same-cohort pre-change baseline; this packet may compare against it but is development evidence only, not blind generalization and not an ARC-AGI-1 or ARC-AGI-2 solver claim. The cohort was selected and source-pinned before task-grid parsing; its baseline was later executed before this implementation. The live controller receives only visible training input/output examples and test inputs. It receives no task ID, imported cohort metadata, GT feature contract, GT solver, historical decomposition, or held-out output before committing a complete grid. P0013 remains an immutable 0/50 frozen negative measurement and is not rerun or rewritten.",
